  "scope": "SCOPE OF THE VALUE HOLD-OUT (\u26d4 quote no row without this). The hold-out is from the STORE'S FIT POOL, not from the encoder, the decoder or the judge. Those three are frozen, hash-pinned and read-only (charter \u00a7A.4) and were fitted on a train split containing EVERY hue and EVERY shape; re-fitting them on a value hold-out would void every wave-2 number and is out of scope. Therefore 'never trained on' means here: THE STORE NEVER HELD A ROW CARRYING THAT VALUE. The decoder can still render the value and the judge can still recognise it \u2014 which is what makes rows 2/5/6/7 scorable at all. \u26d4 Read end-to-end, 'never seen' is false and the claim dies with it."
